Author: vabhzw17eg2qu4m9-bit <vabhzw17eg2qu4m9@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 13 05:46:08 2026 +0300

    fix(1413): composer echo tick check survives mid-run transcript appends (#1492)

    Red run 37774628085 (both widths): the queue drain (one turn per
    filler, fired the moment the busy run ends) hit the exhausted mock
    script, and the CLI's transient-retry ladder printed a
    '[net] connection lost (500: script exhausted) - retrying' notice
    exactly between the two sampled frames - 5 changed rows instead of 1.
    Red run 37711572647 (100x40) was the pre-#1374 face-width-sensitive
    mask (row.indexOf(' ')) tripping on a mid-window face swap; already
    fixed at main by the kKaomojiFaceZoneCells mask.

    Deterministic fix, test-only:
    - script every queue-drain turn (33 acks + spares) so the mock can
      never exhaust and the retry ladder can never arm, whichever failure
      mode ends the busy run early (run 37774628085's shard also showed
      the bash tool dying instantly with 'Cannot modify an unmodifiable
      list', which ended the probe turn at once);
    - keep the probe busy 55s (under the #1349 bare-sleep 60s denial) so
      the drain cannot start while the frames are compared;
    - scope the ticker-in-place contract to the pinned block from the
      ticker row down (queue chrome, input row, footer byte-static; the
      ticker moves only face + seconds and actually ticks), and tolerate
      legitimate transcript appends above it - a #496-class regression
      still trips, an environment append no longer aborts the check.

    Co-authored-by: sm-silent-update <sm-silent-update@users.noreply.github.com>

